Policy</div><div><br></div><div>Background:</div><div>https://nsa.2026.act=
ion.cr.yp.to</div><div>https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/FsbYnIjn=
GGX4Eek5DuUiZpc3cBI/</div><div><br></div><div>The list archive is =
public.</div><div>To avoid spam, illegal content, and&nbsp;disruption of =
list operations, the mailing list is moderated (usually on a daily =
basis).</div><div><br></div><div><div>This mailing list operates as an =
independent private initiative. There is no =
affiliation.</div><div><br></div><div>It operates independently of the =
Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) and is neither provided by, nor =
endorsed by, the IETF. Views expressed here are not official IETF =
positions.</div></div><div><br></div><div>IETF is a registered =
trademark. For details, see: =
https://trustee.ietf.org/assets/trademarks-and-logos/</div><div>Usage =
here follows the IETF guidelines: "The acronym =E2=80=9CIETF=E2=80=9D =
may be used factually in any online or traditional publication, in =
presentations and documents, and in press and media reports, as a =
descriptive term for the Internet Engineering Task Force." =
(https://trustee.ietf.org/about/faq/#logo-acronym, October 15, =
2026.)</div></div><div style=3D"caret-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, =
